 "id": "cases/evolve-iter-15ma",
 "type": "fyo:ScenarioSpecification",
 "title": {
  "zh": "ITER 15 MA 感应燃烧（解析几何，自足）",
  "en": "ITER 15 MA inductive burn (analytic geometry, self-contained)"
 },
 "note": {
  "zh": "★**不需要任何外部文件**：形状是解析的（a = 2.0 m、R/a = 3.1、κ = 1.86、δ = 0.48、B<sub>0</sub> = 5.3 T），所以这一档随页面就能跑。代价写在页面规矩里：解析几何定不出 ⟨|∇ρ|²/R²⟩，**电流道因此禁用**，q 是规定的、锯齿也就无从触发。要电流道与锯齿，用下面那一档（导入参考平衡）或换到装置几何。★**边界温度 3 keV 是台基顶，不是刮削层**：梯子停在 ψ_N = 0.95，Dirichlet 点就是台基顶。3.000 keV 不是随手取的——ASTRA 的 ITER 参考剖面恰在 x = 0.948 处过 3.008 keV（`tests/data/reference/iter15ma_astra_burn.csv`，逐条对拍在 `docs/note/iter-15ma-benchmark.md`）。★**台基模型自 v112 起是有的**（EPED1-NN，勾「台基模型」那一格），这一档默认关着；**开着时它现在给 T<sub>ped</sub> = 3.617 keV（p<sub>ped</sub> 81.1 kPa、Δψ 0.034）**——正落在内核那条 ITER 测试要求的区间里，也正中已发表的 EPED1 基线（~79 kPa / 0.033 / 3.5 keV）。★★**2026-08-24：形状与成分按三处一致的来源改过了**（此前是 κ 1.70 / δ 0.34 / 台基顶密度 3.0×10<sup>19</sup> / Z<sub>eff</sub> 1.20，那一组只对得上「95 % 值」而非边界值）。**新的一组**：κ = 1.86 · δ = 0.48 · 台基顶 n<sub>e</sub> = 7.0×10<sup>19</sup> · Z<sub>eff</sub> = 2.00。**三处来源**：内核自己的 ITER 验证常量（`rust/fylite/src/pedestal.rs` 的 `const ITER`：δ 0.485 · κ 1.85 · n_ped 7.0）、FUSE 的 `case_parameters(:ITER; init_from=:scalars, **boundary_from=:scalars**)`（δ 0.485 · κ 1.85 · n_ped = 0.9×0.75×n<sub>G</sub> = 7.008×10<sup>19</sup> · Z<sub>eff</sub> 2.0）、以及 ASTRA 参考剖面在台基顶的 9.654×10<sup>19</sup>（同量级）。逐项对照见 `docs/note/fuse-cases.md` §5。★成分：**氖 1.10 % 隐含 Z<sub>eff</sub> = 1.99，与控件上的 2.00 对得上**——读数里那两个数就是给你核这件事的。**换成氖是 Z<sub>eff</sub> = 2.0 的连带**：铍要到 Z<sub>eff</sub> 2.0 得 5 % 以上，既超出滑杆量程也不是这台机器的做法，而**氖正是 FUSE 那一档用的杂质**。（FUSE 还带 5 % 氦灰，本栏没有氦灰这一格，**差着**。）燃料占比 0.375 是 ITER 自己的稀释（n<sub>D</sub> = n<sub>T</sub> = 0.375 n<sub>e</sub>），α 功率按 f² 走，这一项差 1.8 倍。★χ₀ = 0.6 m²/s <strong>不是这一档调出来的</strong>：它来自下面那一档的参考对标，原样搬来。跑到 8 s 时这一档给出 W<sub>th</sub> ≈ **356 MJ**、τ<sub>E</sub> ≈ **4.9 s**、β<sub>N</sub> ≈ **1.77**、Q ≈ **11.3**（T<sub>e</sub>(0) ≈ 23.3 keV、P<sub>α</sub> 74.5 MW）—— W<sub>th</sub>、β<sub>N</sub> 与 Q 都在 ITER 15 MA 的设计点上；**τ<sub>E</sub> 偏高是氖辐射的连带**（总辐射 34.7 MW，其中非韧致 10.4 MW，而 τ<sub>E</sub> = W/(P<sub>in</sub>−P<sub>rad</sub>)）。★χ₀ 随这次修正从 0.6 重定为 **0.40**：形状、密度与成分都换了，旧的那个 0.6 是在旧输入上取的。★★它<strong>还在往上走</strong>（dW/dt > 0），而且不会停：常数 χ 对加热功率<strong>没有响应</strong>，于是这个模型里没有燃烧自控——温度升→α 功率升→温度再升。这不是数值发散，是这条闭包的物理后果，也正是「常数 χ 不是预测型闭包」的现场。★<strong>步长受电子—离子交换时标约束</strong>：交换项是显式进算符的，步长长过交换时间不会炸，会让两条热道<strong>悄悄解耦</strong>（本档实测过：自适应把 dt 涨到 0.13 s，T<sub>e</sub> 11.8 keV 对 T<sub>i</sub> 6.3 keV，α 功率只有一半）。所以这一档用固定 dt = 20 ms，页面另有一道以交换时标封顶的闸，封了多少步报在读数里。 ★★<strong>2026-08-24 更正：上面那句 FUSE 的出处要指名分支。</strong>`boundary_from` 缺省是 `:auto`，而 `:auto` 在 `init_from` 不是 `:ods` 时解到的是 **`:MXH_params`**，不是 `:scalars`——所以只写 `init_from=:scalars` 时 FUSE 用的边界是 MXH 数组，κ = 1.8458、δ = sin(s₁) = sin(0.4532) = <strong>0.4379</strong>（`mxh.δ == sin(mxh.s[1])`，MillerExtendedHarmonic.jl v2.1.2 `src/MXH.jl:54`）。δ 0.485 / κ 1.85 那一对要显式传 `boundary_from=:scalars` 才走得到。<strong>这一档的 κ 1.86 / δ 0.48 站的是内核自己的 `const ITER`（δ 0.485 · κ 1.85）</strong>，那一条没变；变的是 FUSE 这一条旁证要说清是哪个分支——两个分支的 δ 差着 10 %。MXH 那一支自成一档，在菜单里叫 <code>FUSE · ITER（输入对照，不是 FUSE 的答案）</code>，由 `tools/fuse-case-to-fylite.py` 生成。",
  "en": "★**No external file needed**: the shape is analytic (a = 2.0 m, R/a = 3.1, kappa = 1.86, delta = 0.48, B0 = 5.3 T), so this case runs as the page opens. The price is the page's own rule: analytic geometry does not determine gm2, so the **current channel is disabled**, q is prescribed and no sawtooth can be triggered. For those, use the case below (import a reference equilibrium) or switch to device geometry. ★**The 3 keV boundary is the pedestal top, not the scrape-off layer**: the ladder stops at psi_N = 0.95 and the Dirichlet point IS the pedestal top; 3.000 keV is where the ASTRA ITER reference profile passes at x = 0.948. ★**A pedestal model exists since v112** (EPED1-NN); this case leaves it off, but **with it on it now gives T_ped = 3.617 keV (p_ped 81.1 kPa, Δψ 0.034)** — inside the band the kernel's own ITER test requires and on the published EPED1 baseline (~79 kPa / 0.033 / 3.5 keV). ★★**2026-08-24: the shape and composition were corrected to the set three sources agree on** (they were kappa 1.70 / delta 0.34 / pedestal-top n_e 3.0e19 / Z_eff 1.20 — a set that matches 95 % values, not boundary values). **The new set**: kappa = 1.86, delta = 0.48, pedestal-top n_e = 7.0e19, Z_eff = 2.00. **The three sources**: the kernel's own ITER validation constant (`rust/fylite/src/pedestal.rs`, `const ITER`: delta 0.485, kappa 1.85, n_ped 7.0); FUSE's `case_parameters(:ITER; init_from=:scalars, **boundary_from=:scalars**)` (delta 0.485, kappa 1.85, n_ped = 0.9*0.75*n_G = 7.008e19, Z_eff 2.0); and ASTRA's pedestal-top 9.654e19 (same order). Item-by-item in `docs/note/fuse-cases.md` §5. ★**A pedestal model has existed since v112** (EPED1-NN, the pedestal checkbox), but **this case leaves it off** and the edge stays the number you give — for the reason below. ★★**Two conventions stated plainly (T-C6 / T-C8), because they bite**: 〔one〕 the edge-density control lands at the ladder end, i.e. the **pedestal top**, and this case fills it with **3.0e19, ASTRA's *separatrix* density**, where ASTRA's pedestal top is 9.654e19 — 68.9 % lower. **chi_0 = 0.6 was taken on that low density**; raise it to 9.7 and the same chi_0 gives Q = 5.6, while the ASTRA benchmark pins **chi_0 ~ 0.43**. 〔two〕 the pedestal path is fed this case's **delta_95 = 0.34 and kappa_95 = 1.70** and the **volume-average Z_eff = 1.2**, whereas the kernel's own ITER validation constant uses the **boundary shape delta = 0.485, kappa = 1.85 and pedestal Z_eff = 1.8** — same kernel, same density, 25 % apart in p_ped, enough to push T_ped below the band the kernel's own test requires. **Both are measured and neither was quietly fixed: changing them means re-deriving chi_0 and the four headline numbers, i.e. a different case.** ★Composition: **neon at 1.10 % implies Z_eff = 1.99 against the control's 2.00** — the two numbers in the readings are there for you to check exactly that. **Switching to neon is a consequence of Z_eff = 2.0**: beryllium would need over 5 %, past the slider and not what this machine does, and **neon is what FUSE's case uses**. (FUSE also carries 5 % helium ash; this bar has no helium-ash control — that one **differs**.) ★chi0 = 0.6 m^2/s was <strong>not tuned here</strong>: it comes from the reference benchmark in the case below, carried over unchanged. At 8 s this case gives W_th about 342 MJ, tau_E about 3.6 s, beta_N about 1.8 and Q about 11 -- the same order as the ITER 15 MA design point, and none of those numbers was fitted. ★★It is <strong>still rising</strong> (dW/dt > 0) and it will not stop: a constant chi has <strong>no response to the heating power</strong>, so this model has no burn control -- hotter gives more alpha power gives hotter. That is not a numerical divergence but a consequence of the closure, and it is precisely what “a constant chi is not a predictive closure” looks like. ★<strong>The step is bounded by the electron-ion exchange time</strong>: the exchange reaches the operator explicitly, and a step longer than that time does not blow up -- it <strong>decouples the heat pair silently</strong> (measured on this case: the adaptive controller grew dt to 0.13 s and reported T_e = 11.8 keV beside T_i = 6.3 keV, with half the alpha power). So this case uses a fixed dt of 20 ms, and the page carries a cap at the exchange time whose count is reported in the readings. ★★<strong>2026-08-24 correction: the FUSE citation above must name the branch.</strong> `boundary_from` defaults to `:auto`, and for any `init_from` other than `:ods` that resolves to **`:MXH_params`**, not `:scalars` — so with `init_from=:scalars` alone FUSE's boundary is the MXH array, kappa = 1.8458 and delta = sin(s1) = sin(0.4532) = <strong>0.4379</strong> (`mxh.δ == sin(mxh.s[1])`, MillerExtendedHarmonic.jl v2.1.2 `src/MXH.jl:54`). The 0.485 / 1.85 pair needs an explicit `boundary_from=:scalars`. <strong>This case's kappa 1.86 / delta 0.48 rest on the kernel's own `const ITER` (delta 0.485, kappa 1.85)</strong>, which is unchanged; what changes is that the FUSE corroboration has to name its branch — the two differ by 10 % in delta. The MXH branch is its own case in the menu, <code>FUSE · ITER (inputs only, not FUSE's answer)</code>, generated by `tools/fuse-case-to-fylite.py`."
 },
 "prescribed_task_kind": "fyo:PhysicsModelingTask",
